  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nChickasaw County, Iowa - County Government Services\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Bid Notices\n Calendar\n\n Courts\n\n Employment\n FAQ\n \n\n Translate Language\n \n Translate\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n Home\n \n\n Departments \n \n\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor\n Board of Supervisors\n Conservation\n Emergency Management / NG911\n EMS\n Engineer's Office and Secondary Roads\n Environmental Health\n General Assistance\n Land Use\n Public Health and Home Care Services\n Recorder/Registrar\n Rural Recycling\n Sheriff\n Treasurer\n Veteran Affairs\n \n \n \n\n About \n \n\n Boards and Commissions\n Cemeteries\n Communities\n Elected Officials\n School Districts\n Township Information\n Tourism\n \n \n Contact\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Clear · 46°\n \n \n \n \n\n Find departments, services, staff, and more\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Elections \n \n \n\n \n \n Meetings & Agendas \n \n \n\n \n \n Pay Property Taxes \n \n \n\n \n \n 2026 Directory \n \n \n\n \n \n Renew Vehicle Tags \n \n \n\n \n \n GIS Mapping \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nWhat's Happening\n \n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n CHICKASAW COUNTY COMMISSION AND BOARD MEMBER OPENINGS\n \n posted 9/28/26\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n DRESDEN TOWNSHIP MEETING\n \n posted 9/15/26\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n FREE Radon Test Kits\n \n posted 8/24/26\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n Help us rebuild Iowa Bridges!\n \n posted 7/16/26\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n Job Opening: Driver- CPR Certified (Part-time/PRN)\n \n posted 1/27/26\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n Job Opening: Advanced EMT ( AEMT)\n \n posted 4/24/25\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n Job Opening: EMT\n \n posted 4/24/25\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n Job Opening: Paramedic/Nurse Exception\n \n posted 4/24/25\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n News Employment Bid Notices Notifications\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nStay Connected\n \n \n\n \n\n \nOctober 19\n \n \n\n Monday \n \n \nVoter Pre-Registration Deadline- 2026 General Election \n \nChickasaw County Courthouse - Auditors Office \n \n\n \nVoter Pre-Registration Deadline- 2026 General Election \n October 19, 2026\n \n\nChickasaw County Courthouse - Auditors Office \n\nVoter Pre-Registration Deadline \n \n\nThe deadlime to pre-register to vote for the General Election is 5:00 pm. This applies to registration in person (including registration at driver's license stations or agencies) or by mail. Voters may register online until 11:59p.m. \n \n\nExceptions: Mailed registration forms postmarked on or before 10/19/2026 are considered on time even if they are received after 5 p.m. today. \n \n\nAfter today, a person may register to vote at the auditor's office and vote an absentee ballot. The process is the same as for registerin gto vote on election day. \n \n\nAuditors office will be open until 5 p.m.\n \n\n \n \n\n \nOctober 21\n \n \n\n Wednesday \n \n \nVeterans Coffee Club\n \n\n 8:30 a.m. \nHeritage Center \n \n\n \nVeterans Coffee Club\n October 21, 2026\n \n8:30 a.m. \n\nHeritage Center \n\nVeterans of Chickasaw County, Mark it on your calander, every 3rd Wednesday! \n \n\nYou and your spouse are invited to come visit with other Veterans over a hot cup of coffee. \n \n\nRemember, please tell other Veterans of the event, after all, \"word of mouth is the best advertisement\" \n \n\nThank you\n \n\n \n \n\n \nOctober 28\n \n \n\n Wednesday \n \n \nPublic Testing of Voting Equipment – General Election\n \nChickasaw County Courthouse - Auditors Office \n \n\n \nPublic Testing of Voting Equipment – General Election\n October 28, 2026\n \n\nChickasaw County Courthouse - Auditors Office \n\nPublic Testing of Voting Equipment – General Election\n \nThe Chickasaw County Auditor's Office will conduct public testing of voting equipment to verify that all voting systems are functioning properly and accurately recording votes prior to the November 3, 2026, General Election. The public is welcome to attend.\n \n\n \n \n\n \nNovember 2\n \n \n\n Monday \n \n \nAbsentee Ballot In- Person Deadline\n \nChickasaw County Courthouse - Auditors Office \n \n\n \nAbsentee Ballot In- Person Deadline\n November 2, 2026\n \n\nChickasaw County Courthouse - Auditors Office \n\nAbsentee Ballot- In Person Deadline \n \n\nLast day to request and vote an absentee ballot in person at the auditor's office\n \n\n \n\n \n2026 GENERAL ELECTION DAY\n November 3, 2026\n \n\nChickasaw County Courthouse - Auditors Office \n\n2026 GENERAL ELECTION DAY\n \nTuesday, November 3, 2026 – Polls are open from 7:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. Eligible registered voters may cast their ballot at their designated polling place. Voters who need to register or update their registration may do so at their polling place by providing proof of identity and proof of residence as required by Iowa law\n \n\n \n \n\n Calendar\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nChickasaw County, Iowa \n \n\nLocated in northeast Iowa, Chickasaw County was established in 1851, named after the Chickasaw tribe, which then lived in the southern United States. It's home to nine cities and 12,012 residents. \n \n\nThe County is administered by a five-member Board of Supervisors who are elected for four-year terms. Other elected officials include the Attorney, Auditor, Recorder, Sheriff, and Treasurer. \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nChickasaw County Courthouse\n\n 8 E Prospect St\n\n New Hampton, IA 50659\n\n Contact Us\n \nCourthouse Hours\n\n M - F 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\n\n Department Hours May Very\nClosed Holidays\n\n \n \nDriver's License Hours\n\n By appointment only.\n\n Call 641-394-3204 to schedule.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n©2026 Chickasaw County, Iowa\n \npowered by \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nVETERANS DAY (November 11, 2026)\n \nTHANKSGIVING (November 26, 2026)\n \nDAY AFTER THANKSGIVING (FRIDAY) (November 27, 2026)\n \nCHRISTMAS EVE DAY (December 24, 2026)\n \nCHRISTMAS DAY (December 25, 2026)\n \nNEW YEAR'S DAY (January 1, 2027)\n \nPRESIDENTS' DAY (February 15, 2027)\n \nGOOD FRIDAY CLOSING @12:00 pm (March 26, 2027)\n \nMEMORIAL DAY (May 31, 2027)\n \nIndependence Day (day after, Monday) (July 5, 2027)\n \n\n\n\n"
